Graphics acceleration for QEMU 11.1 on macOS, ported from UTM's QEMU 10.0.12
(github.com/utmapp/qemu, v10.0.12-utm).

- SPICE GL on macOS: the display renders through ANGLE (or CGL for gl=core) into an
  IOSurface that the local SPICE client draws, and Metal textures from virglrenderer go
  to it directly (ui/spice-display.c, ui/spice-display-metal.m, ui/egl-helpers.c).
- virtio-gpu: native Metal scanouts, the Neptune (Direct3D) context, a fence for a dead
  renderer context, and suspended commands kept at the head of the queue.
- virtio-ramfb and virtio-ramfb-gl: a ramfb console until the guest's virtio-gpu
  driver takes over, which Windows needs.
- console: native scanout textures with a cleanup callback, and a stuck GL block that
  is released instead of stalling the guest's GPU.
- Linux-only dmabuf paths are left as QEMU 11 has them, behind CONFIG_GBM. A remote SPICE
  client with GL is not supported.
- Only the configuration scripts/build-qemu.sh builds is ported: the GTK, SDL, Cocoa and
  D-Bus displays don't build with this patch.

